
Creates a new instance and sets the property values for the new instance.
USAGE:

CREATE <assign list>
NOTE: <assign list> can be more than one property name separated by commas.
Each property name should be followed by '=' and its value.

NOTE: Create cannot be used to create a new class.

The following properties are available:
Property				Type			Operation
========				====			=========
ActiveInputVoltage                 	N/A                 	N/A       
Availability                       	N/A                 	N/A       
BatteryInstalled                   	N/A                 	N/A       
CanTurnOffRemotely                 	N/A                 	N/A       
CommandFile                        	N/A                 	N/A       
ConfigManagerErrorCode             	N/A                 	N/A       
ConfigManagerUserConfig            	N/A                 	N/A       
Description                        	N/A                 	N/A       
DeviceID                           	N/A                 	N/A       
ErrorCleared                       	N/A                 	N/A       
ErrorDescription                   	N/A                 	N/A       
EstimatedChargeRemaining           	N/A                 	N/A       
EstimatedRunTime                   	N/A                 	N/A       
FirstMessageDelay                  	N/A                 	N/A       
InstallDate                        	N/A                 	N/A       
IsSwitchingSupply                  	N/A                 	N/A       
LastErrorCode                      	N/A                 	N/A       
LowBatterySignal                   	N/A                 	N/A       
MessageInterval                    	N/A                 	N/A       
Name                               	N/A                 	N/A       
PNPDeviceID                        	N/A                 	N/A       
PowerFailSignal                    	N/A                 	N/A       
PowerManagementCapabilities        	N/A                 	N/A       
PowerManagementSupported           	N/A                 	N/A       
Range1InputFrequencyHigh           	N/A                 	N/A       
Range1InputFrequencyLow            	N/A                 	N/A       
Range1InputVoltageHigh             	N/A                 	N/A       
Range1InputVoltageLow              	N/A                 	N/A       
Range2InputFrequencyHigh           	N/A                 	N/A       
Range2InputFrequencyLow            	N/A                 	N/A       
Range2InputVoltageHigh             	N/A                 	N/A       
Range2InputVoltageLow              	N/A                 	N/A       
RemainingCapacityStatus            	N/A                 	N/A       
Status                             	N/A                 	N/A       
StatusInfo                         	N/A                 	N/A       
TimeOnBackup                       	N/A                 	N/A       
TotalOutputPower                   	N/A                 	N/A       
TypeOfRangeSwitching               	N/A                 	N/A       
UPSPort                            	N/A                 	N/A       

